{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some MCP clients still speak only spec 2025. Spec 2025 can use sessions, and a session lives in one process. On a deploy with many instances, sessions need sticky routing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMCPServer"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps no spec 2025 session, so any instance can answer any request. Set the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessions"},{"type":"text","value":" option only when you need something else:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'stateless'"},{"type":"text","value":" (the default): no session. It works on any host."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'memory'"},{"type":"text","value":": sessions in the process. The server can ask a spec 2025 client for input or a sample."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'reject'"},{"type":"text","value":": spec 2026 only."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"serve-spec-2025-without-sessions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Serve spec 2025 without sessions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You do not have to set anything. A new server answers each spec 2025 request, and no session is kept. A spec 2026 client sends no session id either, so any instance can serve both."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without a session, the server cannot send a request back to a spec 2025 client. For that client:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" throws an error that names the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessions"},{"type":"text","value":" option."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.sample"},{"type":"text","value":" calls the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"},{"type":"text","value":" option of the server. Without that option, it throws."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A spec 2026 client gets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"},{"type":"text","value":" with no session."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-sessions-for-input-and-sampling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep sessions for input and sampling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To ask a spec 2025 client for input or a sample, set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessions"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'memory'"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  sessions: 'memory',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serveMCPStdio"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'memory'"},{"type":"text","value":" when you do not set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessions"},{"type":"text","value":". A stdio process serves one client, so a session costs nothing there."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"route-each-session-to-one-instance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route each session to one instance"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A spec 2025 session keeps a live connection object. That object stays in the process that opened the session. Another process cannot read it."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client sends the session id on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mcp-session-id"},{"type":"text","value":" header."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A request with an unknown session id gets 404 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Session not found"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On a deploy with more than one instance, a later request can reach an instance that did not open the session. That request gets 404. Use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mcp-session-id"},{"type":"text","value":" header as the key for sticky routing on your load balancer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"when-a-session-closes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a session closes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A session closes in two cases:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DELETE"},{"type":"text","value":" with its session id."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The session gets no request for 30 minutes."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server checks for idle sessions when a request comes in. After a session closes, the client must open a new session."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server has no limit on the number of open sessions. Each session stays in memory until it closes, which can take 30 minutes. On a public server, set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"auth"},{"type":"text","value":", or limit new sessions at your proxy."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sessions-and-auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sessions and auth"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the server has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"auth"},{"type":"text","value":", the session belongs to the caller that opened it: the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clientId"},{"type":"text","value":" of the token plus its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sub"},{"type":"text","value":" claim. A request from another caller gets 404, the same as an unknown id. "},{"type":"link","href":"./server-auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Server Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":" shows how the verifier sets them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"turn-spec-2025-off","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Turn spec 2025 off"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To serve spec 2026 only, set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessions"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'reject'"},{"type":"text","value":". A spec 2025 request then gets the SDK rejection. A client that speaks only spec 2025 cannot use that server."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  sessions: 'reject',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each spec 2025 client now gets the behavior that you chose."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"serve-spec-2025-without-sessions","text":"Serve spec 2025 without sessions","level":2},{"id":"keep-sessions-for-input-and-sampling","text":"Keep sessions for input and sampling","level":2},{"id":"route-each-session-to-one-instance","text":"Route each session to one instance","level":3},{"id":"when-a-session-closes","text":"When a session closes","level":3},{"id":"sessions-and-auth","text":"Sessions and auth","level":3},{"id":"turn-spec-2025-off","text":"Turn spec 2025 off","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nSome MCP clients still speak only spec 2025. Spec 2025 can use sessions, and a session lives in one process. On a deploy with many instances, sessions need sticky routing.\n\nBy default, `createMCPServer` keeps no spec 2025 session, so any instance can answer any request. Set the `sessions` option only when you need something else:\n\n- `'stateless'` (the default): no session. It works on any host.\n- `'memory'`: sessions in the process. The server can ask a spec 2025 client for input or a sample.\n- `'reject'`: spec 2026 only.\n\n## Serve spec 2025 without sessions\n\nYou do not have to set anything. A new server answers each spec 2025 request, and no session is kept. A spec 2026 client sends no session id either, so any instance can serve both.\n\nWithout a session, the server cannot send a request back to a spec 2025 client. For that client:\n\n- `ctx.context.requestInput` throws an error that names the `sessions` option.\n- `ctx.context.sample` calls the `sample` option of the server. Without that option, it throws.\n\nA spec 2026 client gets `requestInput` and `sample` with no session.\n\n## Keep sessions for input and sampling\n\nTo ask a spec 2025 client for input or a sample, set `sessions` to `'memory'`:\n\n```ts\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  sessions: 'memory',\n})\n```\n\n`serveMCPStdio` uses `'memory'` when you do not set `sessions`. A stdio process serves one client, so a session costs nothing there.\n\n### Route each session to one instance\n\nA spec 2025 session keeps a live connection object. That object stays in the process that opened the session. Another process cannot read it.\n\n- The client sends the session id on the `mcp-session-id` header.\n- A request with an unknown session id gets 404 `Session not found`.\n\nOn a deploy with more than one instance, a later request can reach an instance that did not open the session. That request gets 404. Use the `mcp-session-id` header as the key for sticky routing on your load balancer.\n\n### When a session closes\n\nA session closes in two cases:\n\n- The client sends `DELETE` with its session id.\n- The session gets no request for 30 minutes.\n\nThe server checks for idle sessions when a request comes in. After a session closes, the client must open a new session.\n\nThe server has no limit on the number of open sessions. Each session stays in memory until it closes, which can take 30 minutes. On a public server, set `auth`, or limit new sessions at your proxy.\n\n### Sessions and auth\n\nWhen the server has `auth`, the session belongs to the caller that opened it: the `clientId` of the token plus its `sub` claim. A request from another caller gets 404, the same as an unknown id. [MCP Server Auth](./server-auth) shows how the verifier sets them.\n\n## Turn spec 2025 off\n\nTo serve spec 2026 only, set `sessions` to `'reject'`. A spec 2025 request then gets the SDK rejection. A client that speaks only spec 2025 cannot use that server.\n\n```ts\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  sessions: 'reject',\n})\n```\n\nEach spec 2025 client now gets the behavior that you chose.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: MCP Server Sessions\nid: mcp-server-sessions\norder: 13\ndescription: \"Choose how a createMCPServer server serves spec 2025 clients: with no session, with sessions for input and sampling, or not at all.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - mcp\n  - model context protocol\n  - createMCPServer\n  - sticky sessions\n  - spec 2025\n  - mcp-session-id\n---\n\nSome MCP clients still speak only spec 2025. Spec 2025 can use sessions, and a session lives in one process. On a deploy with many instances, sessions need sticky routing.\n\nBy default, `createMCPServer` keeps no spec 2025 session, so any instance can answer any request. Set the `sessions` option only when you need something else:\n\n- `'stateless'` (the default): no session. It works on any host.\n- `'memory'`: sessions in the process. The server can ask a spec 2025 client for input or a sample.\n- `'reject'`: spec 2026 only.\n\n## Serve spec 2025 without sessions\n\nYou do not have to set anything. A new server answers each spec 2025 request, and no session is kept. A spec 2026 client sends no session id either, so any instance can serve both.\n\nWithout a session, the server cannot send a request back to a spec 2025 client. For that client:\n\n- `ctx.context.requestInput` throws an error that names the `sessions` option.\n- `ctx.context.sample` calls the `sample` option of the server. Without that option, it throws.\n\nA spec 2026 client gets `requestInput` and `sample` with no session.\n\n## Keep sessions for input and sampling\n\nTo ask a spec 2025 client for input or a sample, set `sessions` to `'memory'`:\n\n```ts\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  sessions: 'memory',\n})\n```\n\n`serveMCPStdio` uses `'memory'` when you do not set `sessions`. A stdio process serves one client, so a session costs nothing there.\n\n### Route each session to one instance\n\nA spec 2025 session keeps a live connection object. That object stays in the process that opened the session. Another process cannot read it.\n\n- The client sends the session id on the `mcp-session-id` header.\n- A request with an unknown session id gets 404 `Session not found`.\n\nOn a deploy with more than one instance, a later request can reach an instance that did not open the session. That request gets 404. Use the `mcp-session-id` header as the key for sticky routing on your load balancer.\n\n### When a session closes\n\nA session closes in two cases:\n\n- The client sends `DELETE` with its session id.\n- The session gets no request for 30 minutes.\n\nThe server checks for idle sessions when a request comes in. After a session closes, the client must open a new session.\n\nThe server has no limit on the number of open sessions. Each session stays in memory until it closes, which can take 30 minutes. On a public server, set `auth`, or limit new sessions at your proxy.\n\n### Sessions and auth\n\nWhen the server has `auth`, the session belongs to the caller that opened it: the `clientId` of the token plus its `sub` claim. A request from another caller gets 404, the same as an unknown id. [MCP Server Auth](./server-auth) shows how the verifier sets them.\n\n## Turn spec 2025 off\n\nTo serve spec 2026 only, set `sessions` to `'reject'`. A spec 2025 request then gets the SDK rejection. A client that speaks only spec 2025 cannot use that server.\n\n```ts\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  sessions: 'reject',\n})\n```\n\nEach spec 2025 client now gets the behavior that you chose.\n"}
